If `this.spawnTimer` starts 0, at t=0 set interval ~0.9, spawn 1. After .9s spawn 1, etc. 90/0.9=100 events, count 2 after 72s → 100+28=128. That matches 132! Ah, because interval average ~0.9 not .75 due to RNG range 0.72-1.25 average .985 and base .767 → .755, but perhaps time in formula uses `this.time` at event and `interval` maybe .9 because time? At 90 base .767; still .755. 90/.755=119 events; count 2 after 72 → 119 + 47 = 166. But 132. Maybe rng avg higher? .985. Hmm.

Actually `count = 1 + Math.floor(this.time / 72)` at 72s: 2; 18s of count2 = 24 extra; events ~108 → 132. So interval ~0.83. Fine. Spawn rate ~1.5/s; that's low for VS feel. At 90s only 132 spawns, 67 kills, 77 alive; screen has maybe 20 visible, rest offscreen approaching. It's okay but we want more density. Increase spawn rate: base interval `0.7 - time*0.0015` clamp .14; count `1 + floor(time/50)`; initial waves. At 90: base .565*avg .985=.556 → 162 events; count 2 after 50 → +? 90/0.556=162 events; first 50s 90 events, next 40s 72*2=144 → 234 spawns. Better. At 300: base .25*avg=.246 → 1220 events * count 7 → huge; cap 280. Fine. Need tune to 100-200 enemies by 5 min. With cap 280, spawn fills. Good.

But performance with 280 enemies and rendering okay. Let's increase:
```js
const interval = clamp(0.7 - time*0.0014, 0.13, 0.8) * rng(0.7,1.2);
